## 5. Module 4 Deep-Dive — Lakehouse Storage & Version Control

### 5.1 Palantir Benchmark: Version Control as Core Infrastructure

All scheduled pipeline workflows in Foundry are fully version-controlled (citation:18). Our storage layer SHALL implement a complete lakehouse architecture with Iceberg as the table format.

### 5.2 Iceberg Table Management

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              ICEBERG TABLE OPERATIONS                             │
│                                                                  │
│  Supported Operations:                                           │
│                                                                  │
│  1. APPEND: Add new rows (most common for pipelines)             │
│     Iceberg: Data file append + new snapshot                     │
│     Atomicity: Yes (snapshot-level)                              │
│                                                                  │
│  2. OVERWRITE: Replace all rows (full refresh)                   │
│     Iceberg: New data files + delete old files in new snapshot   │
│     Atomicity: Yes                                               │
│                                                                  │
│  3. DELETE: Remove specific rows                                 │
│     Iceberg: Position delete files or equality delete files      │
│     Atomicity: Yes                                               │
│                                                                  │
│  4. MERGE (Upsert): Insert or update based on key                │
│     Iceberg: MERGE INTO SQL support                              │
│     Atomicity: Yes                                               │
│                                                                  │
│  5. SCHEMA UPDATE: Add/rename columns, widen types              │
│     Iceberg: Schema evolution with schema ID tracking            │
│     Atomicity: Yes                                               │
│     Compatibility: Additive only (no breaking changes)           │
│                                                                  │
│  6. PARTITION EVOLUTION: Change partition scheme                  │
│     Iceberg: Hidden partitioning, partition evolution             │
│     Atomicity: Yes                                               │
│                                                                  │
│  TIME TRAVEL:                                                    │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ Query by snapshot ID:                                     │   │
│  │ SELECT * FROM customers_cleaned                           │   │
│  │   FOR SYSTEM_VERSION AS OF 47                             │   │
│  │                                                          │   │
│  │ Query by timestamp:                                       │   │
│  │ SELECT * FROM customers_cleaned                           │   │
│  │   FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF '2026-09-08 02:00:00'            │   │
│  │                                                          │   │
│  │ Diff between versions:                                    │   │
│  │ SELECT * FROM customers_cleaned                           │   │
│  │   CHANGES BETWEEN VERSION 46 AND 47                      │   │
